            <ArticleTitle>Syndrome X: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transmural myocardial infarction occurred in a 48-year-old woman with syndrome X -- atypical angina pectoris and angiographically normal coronary arteries. Before the infarction her electrocardiogram had been normal at rest but showed ischemia after exercise. Angiography 3 months after infarction revealed a normal coronary tree but hypokinesia of the posterior left ventricular wall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
